And people then would say anywhere between one and five cents.

583
00:45:49,120 --> 00:45:52,000
And then we asked them, how much would you sell your sweatcoins for?

584
00:45:52,240 --> 00:45:53,280
And guess what the answer was?

585
00:45:53,680 --> 00:45:54,720
I'm going to guess higher.

586
00:45:55,200 --> 00:46:08,320
fifty cents to a dollar, which means that basically your own steps, or actually I bet, David, the steps of your son are going to be far more important to you than, let's say, my steps or someone else's that you don't even know.

587
00:46:08,640 --> 00:46:09,520
That's really interesting.

588
00:46:10,000 --> 00:46:17,680
Considering it's fully fungible, like, Oh man, that's us like there's an endless possibilities there and we're just scratching the surface there.

589
00:46:17,840 --> 00:46:18,240
Yeah, yeah.

590
00:46:18,320 --> 00:46:22,240
I mean, it tells you you haven't really created a currency because it has no currency, right?

591
00:46:22,400 --> 00:46:23,680
It has no bidirectional trade value.

592
00:46:24,160 --> 00:46:26,160
It's got an asymmetry in bidirectional trade.

593
00:46:26,560 --> 00:46:32,800
A really interesting conversation we had a long time ago when we just started with a dean of one of the top business schools.

594
00:46:32,960 --> 00:46:38,640
And he said, like, I'm not sure that you guys necessarily want to go crypto because then the magic will disappear.

595
00:46:39,040 --> 00:46:44,720
I think actually it's a fair point because there's this discrepancy in that the market value versus the perceived value.

596
00:46:45,360 --> 00:46:45,920
Yeah, yeah.

597
00:46:46,000 --> 00:46:48,640
You don't want to, you don't want to shatter anyone's perception, right?

598
00:46:48,800 --> 00:46:51,200
So I think that's, there's a lot of really interesting stuff.

599
00:46:51,360 --> 00:46:57,200
